OLD_PART_2 = "We collect only what we need, and only when you do something on the site.\n### When you browse\n- Nothing that identifies you. We count visits without cookies (see Cookies, below).\n- If a page breaks, an error report is made. It leaves out names, email addresses and IP addresses, but can include your account's internal number and the type of browser.\n### When you take the guided journey\n- Your answers: when you would come, how often, what you would use, whether you come alone, what you do (and, for property, your link to property and roughly how many properties), how you heard about us, and anything you type in the short text boxes.\n- The membership we suggest, and why.\n- About the visit: the page that linked to us (if any), campaign tags in the link, the kind of device (phone, tablet or computer), and when you started and finished.\nAnswers are saved as you go, even if you stop part way. They carry no name unless you register.\n- Your email address, if you give it. Before the journey shows your suggested membership and price, it asks for your email, with a tick to say Spa 99 may email you about opening. We keep the address with your answers, the date you gave it and the version of this notice in force. If you are signed in, we use your account email instead and do not ask.\n### When you register\n- Your name, email address, UK mobile number, date of birth and password. The password is stored scrambled (hashed), so nobody can read it, including us.\n- That you accepted the men-only policy and this notice (which version), with the dates.\n- Whether you would like news from us by email, and when you told us.\n- The membership you registered for, your account ID, and whether you have confirmed your email.\n- Sign-in records: when you sign in and out, failed attempts, and the IP address and browser used.\n### When you apply for the Gold Card\n- Your name, email address and mobile number.\n- What you do. For property: your link to property and roughly how many properties. Also the area you are based in, your company and role, whether you work with BML, who referred you, and any note you add.\n- Your journey answers, if you took the journey.\n- A potential rating (High, Medium or Low) worked out from your answers, with its reasons.\n- Whether you would like news from us by email, and which version of this notice you accepted.\n- Our decision and, if we approve, the date and the invitation we send you.\n- If our team writes to you about your application (for example to ask a question), a record of that email.\n### When you use the Ask us chat {#chat}\n- What you type to the assistant and its replies, with the time. If you gave your email to see prices, or you are signed in, the chat is linked to it. We do not store your IP address with a chat.\n### Change history\n- Earlier versions of your details (a change history): when your account, registration or Gold Card application changes, we keep the previous version, so we can see what changed and put mistakes right. Passwords are never kept in it.\n### Emails\n- A record of each email we send you: which email, when, and whether it went out.\n- Invitation emails contain a tiny image (a tracking pixel), so we know whether the email was opened. Other emails we send you do not.\n- Emails you send us, kept in our mailbox.\n### Our team\n- When our team use our own tools, we record what they do, with their IP address and browser, to keep the system secure. This covers team accounts only."

OLD_PART_3 = "The law asks us to name a lawful basis for each use. Here they are.\n### To run your account and registration\nCreating your account, keeping your registered membership, confirming your email, resetting your password and writing to you about opening. Basis: a contract with you, or steps you asked us to take before one.\n### To check you can join\nSpa 99 is for men aged 18 and over. We use your date of birth and your acceptance of the men-only policy to check this. Basis: steps before a contract, and our legitimate interest in running the spa as described.\n### To suggest a membership and plan the spa\nYour journey answers give you a suggestion. Added together with everyone else's, they show us which times and rooms matter most. Those figures are totals, never decisions about you. Basis: legitimate interests.\n### To consider a Gold Card application\nWe read your application, and the potential rating helps us. Our team may email you with questions about it. The rating never decides on its own: a person does. Basis: steps before a contract, and legitimate interests.\n### To send news, only if you ask\nWe send news by email only if you said yes. You can stop it at any time in My Spa 99, or by writing to {contact}. Basis: your consent.\n### To email you about opening after the journey\nIf you gave your email in the guided journey and ticked the box, we use it to send news about the opening and to understand which membership suits people (your answers, linked to your address, show us what people choose). Basis: your consent. You can withdraw it at any time by following the unsubscribe link in any email or by writing to {contact}; we then stop emailing you and delete the address.\n### To answer your questions in the chat\nThe Ask us assistant answers questions about Spa 99 from our own information. It does not make decisions about you. Basis: legitimate interests.\n### To keep the site and your account safe\nSign-in records, limits on repeated attempts, error reports and our team's activity records. Basis: legitimate interests.\n### When the law requires it\nKeeping records we must keep, and answering lawful requests. Basis: legal obligation.\n### If you do not give us your details\nThe guided journey is optional. To register or apply for the Gold Card, we need the details the form asks for; without them we cannot create your account or consider your application. News by email is always optional.\nWe do not sell your information, and we do not use it for advertising."

